.TH VIRTBASE-PVE-REPATCH 8 "" "virtbase-pve-patches" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
virtbase-pve-repatch \- reapply the virtbase-pve-patches Proxmox VE patches
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B virtbase-pve-repatch
.RB [ apply | unapply | status | dry-run-apply | dry-run-unapply ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B virtbase-pve-repatch
brings the patches shipped in
.I /usr/share/virtbase-pve-patches
into the requested state, then classifies every patch as
.BR applied ,
.B pending
or
.B unknown
and writes the result for the Prometheus node_exporter textfile collector.
A patch is
.B unknown
when it no longer fits the installed Proxmox VE version; it cannot be applied
until it is rebased.
.PP
The dpkg file trigger on
.I /usr/share/perl5/PVE
and the daily
.B virtbase-pve-repatch.timer
run
.BR "virtbase-pve-repatch apply" .
The command defaults to
.BR apply .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B apply
Apply every patch that is not applied, and restart pvedaemon and pveproxy if
anything changed.
.TP
.B unapply
Revert every applied patch.
.TP
.B status
Only classify the patches and write the metrics.
.TP
.BR dry-run-apply ", " dry-run-unapply
Check that apply or unapply would succeed, without changing anything.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Variables may also be set in
.IR /etc/default/virtbase-pve-repatch .
.TP
.B TEXTFILE_DIR
Directory the metrics file is written to; the file is skipped when it does not
exist. Default:
.IR /var/lib/prometheus/node-exporter .
.TP
.B METRIC_FILE
Path of the metrics file. Default:
.IR $TEXTFILE_DIR/virtbase_pve_patches.prom .
.TP
.B SKIP_RESTART
If set, pvedaemon and pveproxy are never restarted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every patch ends up in the requested state, 1 when a patch is pending or
unknown afterwards, 64 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/virtbase-pve-patches/patch.sh
Applies, reverts and classifies the patches.
.TP
.I /etc/default/virtbase-pve-repatch
Optional settings, not shipped by the package.
